Initializes the relvaddr field of the .compact_rel entries, so that ld writes the
same bytes at every link.

mips_elf_relocate_section (bfd/elf32-mips.c) builds each .compact_rel entry in a
local `Elf32_crinfo cptrel` and assigns its format, type, dist2to, konst and vaddr,
but never relvaddr: the 19 low bits of the info word get whatever was on the
stack, and two links of the same objects give different files (bn.elf and every
module). The entries are written in the long format, which carries the address in
vaddr; nothing reads relvaddr (the Linux loader does not read .compact_rel at all),
and with 0 the output depends only on the input.

It changes only the .compact_rel of a link; gas, which uses the same bfd, is
built before this patch is applied.

--- a/bfd/elf32-mips.c
+++ b/bfd/elf32-mips.c
@@ -5779,6 +5779,7 @@
 
 		      /* Make an entry of compact relocation info.  */
 		      mips_elf_set_cr_format (cptrel, CRF_MIPS_LONG);
+		      mips_elf_set_cr_relvaddr (cptrel, 0);
 		      cptrel.vaddr = (rel->r_offset
 				      + input_section->output_section->vma
 				      + input_section->output_offset);
@@ -6012,6 +6013,7 @@
 
 	      /* Make an entry of compact relocation info.  */
 	      mips_elf_set_cr_format (cptrel, CRF_MIPS_LONG);
+	      mips_elf_set_cr_relvaddr (cptrel, 0);
 	      cptrel.vaddr = (rel->r_offset
 			      + input_section->output_section->vma
 			      + input_section->output_offset);
